{
 "contract": "uct.converse-eval.cases/1",
 "_": "CLARIFY FIRST, as cases (Studio, 2026-11-18; owner direction: \"always clarify\"). The door asks its own questions (api/data/clarify_questions.json) with no model call when a choice that changes the maths is not settled, one at a time, and reads the member's answer as their first words plus the answer. Each registry question has a case: the request that leaves it open is ASKED (no model call, nothing built), and one of its own choices, sent as the next message, BUILDS in one call. `clarify-kind-then-length` leaves two open: both are asked, in order, and the build is one call. `clarify-nothing-open` says everything and is never asked. The three `clarify-acronym-*` cases are letters that could mean two indicators (DMI, ADL, AD): asked which, never guessed. The two `remembered-*` cases set what the member chose before (`remembers`) and hold the answer to what it must SAY (`says`): the door's 'as you chose before' sentence beside the assistant's own note, and beside a library build. If a later change to the instructions or the planner stops a question, or stops a choice from settling it, a case here fails. `clarify-benchmark` and `clarify-breakout-window` (slice F): relative strength with no symbol is asked which symbol, and a breakout with no number how many bars back; one of the question's own choices then builds in one call. `clarify-stochastic-kind`: the bare word is asked which Stochastic, and the fast one, tapped, builds the library's formula with K smoothing 1.",
 "chart": {
  "sym": "TEST",
  "tf": "D"
 },
